{"name":"Blackberry Black","hex":"#2e2848","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blackberry","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A fruit-bearing shrub of the aggregate species Rubus fruticosus and some hybrids.","The soft fruit borne by this shrub, formed of a black (when ripe) cluster of drupelets."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To gather or forage for blackberries."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blackberry"},{"term":"black","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Absorbing all light and reflecting none; dark and hueless.","Without light."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour/color perceived in the absence of light, but also when no light is reflected, but rather absorbed.","A black dye or pigment."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/black"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blackberry","blocks":[{"text":"A blackberry is an edible fruit produced by many species in the genus Rubus in the family Rosaceae, hybrids among these species within the subgenus Rubus, and hybrids between the subgenera Rubus and Idaeobatus. The taxonomy of blackberries has historically been confused because of hybridization and apomixis so that species have often been grouped together and called species aggregates."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Ripe%2C_ripening%2C_and_green_blackberries.jpg/330px-Ripe%2C_ripening%2C_and_green_blackberries.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blackberry","wikidata":"Q19842373"},{"title":"Black","blocks":[{"text":"Black is a color that results from the absence or complete absorption of visible light. It is an achromatic color, without chroma, like white and grey. It is often used symbolically or figuratively to represent darkness. Black and white have often been used to describe opposites such as good and evil, the Dark Ages versus the Age of Enlightenment, and night versus day. Since the Middle Ages, black has been the symbolic color of solemnity and authority, and for this reason it is still commonly worn by judges and magistrates."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png/330px-Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black","wikidata":"Q23445"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Rubus_fruticosus_Luc_Viatour.JPG/500px-Rubus_fruticosus_Luc_Viatour.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Rubus_fruticosus_Luc_Viatour.JPG/1280px-Rubus_fruticosus_Luc_Viatour.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Rubus_fruticosus_Luc_Viatour.JPG/500px-Rubus_fruticosus_Luc_Viatour.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARubus_fruticosus_Luc_Viatour.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Halved_blackberry_%28Rubus_fruticosus%29.jpg/250px-Halved_blackberry_%28Rubus_fruticosus%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Halved_blackberry_%28Rubus_fruticosus%29.jpg/500px-Halved_blackberry_%28Rubus_fruticosus%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Halved_blackberry_%28Rubus_fruticosus%29.jpg/250px-Halved_blackberry_%28Rubus_fruticosus%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHalved_blackberry_(Rubus_fruticosus).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wik